\ by-rfl (plan FE1g-4; docs/design/FE1G_TACTICS.md 2.4 and 5.3).
\ Lean: theorem refl_p (p : Prop) : p = p := by rfl
\ gives fun (p : Prop) => @Eq.refl.{1} Prop p. Natural LeanForth cannot
\ write Prop yet (plan FE2), and the statement is not elaborated yet
\ (plan FE1e): the text stops at end with error 71, exit 2.
\ tests/front/tactic-basic.fs runs it with a stand-in that gives the
\ statement forall (p : Prop), p = p (whatever the words below say); the
\ kernel accepts it. Theorems whose sides need a library definition
\ unfolded (0 + n = n) need the Meta layer to see the library while a
\ text runs (plan FE1e).
theorem refl_p
  Nat explicit: n
  0 n + n =
:= by
  by-rfl
end refl_p
